[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Fried Liver Attack"]
[Variation "Fried Liver: 7...Ke6"]
[ECO "C57"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "white"]
[Tricks "trap,mate-threat"]
[Themes "king-hunt,f7-pressure"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. Ng5 4... d5 { Black hits the bishop and blocks the diagonal to f7, which is the best reply to 4.Ng5. } (4... Nxe4 5. Bxf7+ 5... Ke7 6. d4 6... h6 7. Nxe4 7... Kxf7) (4... Bc5 5. Nxf7 5... Bxf2+ 6. Kf1 6... Qe7 7. Nxh8 7... d5 8. exd5 8... Nd4 9. d6 9... Qxd6) (4... Be7 5. Nxf7 5... Rf8 6. Nxd8 6... Kxd8) (4... h6 5. Nxf7 5... Qe7 6. Nxh8 6... d5 7. Bxd5 7... Nd4 8. Bf7+ 8... Kd8) (4... d6 5. Nxf7 5... Qe7 6. Nxh8 6... Be6 7. d3 7... Bxc4 8. dxc4 8... Qe6)
5. exd5 5... Nxd5 { Takes the pawn back. It looks natural, and it walks into the Fried Liver. } (5... Nd4 6. c3 6... b5 7. cxd4 7... bxc4 8. dxe5 8... Nd5 9. Qf3 9... Qg5) (5... Ne4 6. Nxe4 6... Nd4 7. c3 7... Qh4 8. d3) (5... b5 6. Bf1 6... Nd4 7. c3 7... Nxd5 8. Nxf7 8... Kxf7 9. cxd4) (5... Nce7 6. d4 6... Bg4 7. f3 7... Bh5)
6. Nxf7 { The sacrifice. The knight takes the pawn that only the king guards, and it forks the queen and the rook. The point is to pull the king out. [%cal Gg5f7] } 6... Kxf7 { Black should take: the king cannot refuse, or White just wins a pawn and more. } (6... Qe7 7. Bxd5 7... Qh4 8. Nxh8 8... Nd4 9. Bf7+ 9... Kd8) (6... Nf4 7. Nxd8 7... Kxd8) (6... Nb6 7. Nxd8 7... Nxc4 8. Nc6) (6... Be6 7. Nxd8 7... Rxd8 8. O-O 8... h5 9. d3) (6... Qf6 7. Bxd5 7... Bc5 8. O-O 8... Rf8) (6... Qd7 7. Nxh8 7... Nf4 8. O-O 8... Nxg2 9. d4 9... Bb4)
7. Qf3+ { Check, and the queen also attacks the knight on d5, which is pinned by the bishop on c4. [%cal Gf3d5,Gc4d5] } 7... Ke6 { The king runs forward. It is the only move that keeps the knight on d5 protected. } (7... Ke7 8. Bxd5 8... Qe8 9. Bxc6 9... Qxc6 10. Qxc6 10... bxc6) (7... Kg8 8. Bxd5+ 8... Qxd5 9. Qxd5+ 9... Be6 10. Qxe6#)
8. Nc3 { Piles up on the pinned knight on d5. Black has to find ...Ncb4, or White wins it. [%cal Gc3d5] } 8... Ncb4 { The best defence: it protects d5 and threatens ...Nxc2+. } (8... Nce7 9. d4 9... c6 10. dxe5) (8... Qd6 9. Nxd5 9... Kd7 10. c3) (8... Kd6 9. Qxd5+ 9... Ke7 10. Qf7+ 10... Kd6 11. Ne4#)
9. O-O { White castles and ignores the threat on c2, because after ...Nxc2 White has strong pressure. Getting the king safe and the rook into play beats grabbing a pawn. } 9... c6 { Gives the king a flight square on d6 and strengthens the pinned knight. } (9... Qf6 10. Bxd5+ 10... Kd7 11. Qe4 11... Bd6) (9... Be7 10. a3 10... Rf8 11. Qe2) (9... Nxc2 10. Bxd5+ 10... Kd6 11. Bb3 11... Nd4 12. Qd5+ 12... Ke7 13. Qxe5+ 13... Be6) (9... Bd6 10. Nxd5 10... Qh4 11. d4) (9... Kd6 10. Bxd5 10... c6) (9... c5 10. a3 10... Kd7 11. Nxd5 11... Nxd5 12. Bxd5 12... Kc7) (9... a6 10. a3 10... Kd7 11. Nxd5 11... Nxd5 12. Qxd5 12... Bd6)
10. d4 { Opens the centre for the bishop on c1 and the rook on f1, while Black's king is still in the middle. [%cal Gd2d4] } 10... Qf6 { Offers a queen trade and pins down the d4 pawn. } (10... Ke7 11. Bg5+ 11... Kd7 12. Bxd8 12... Kxd8) (10... exd4 11. Bxd5+ 11... Nxd5 12. Rfe1+ 12... Kd6 13. Bg5 13... Qd7) (10... Bd6 11. a3 11... exd4 12. axb4 12... dxc3) (10... Qd6 11. Ne4 11... Qe7 12. dxe5) (10... Nc2 11. dxe5 11... Bc5 12. Nxd5 12... cxd5) (10... Na6 11. Rfe1 11... Nb4 12. Nxd5 12... Nxd5 13. Bxd5)
11. Qe2 { Keeps the queens on and avoids a trade, which would end the attack. White has far more pieces ready than Black. } 11... Ke7 { The king steps off the pinned diagonal at last. } (11... Qg6 12. f4 12... Kd6 13. f5 13... Qe8 14. Bxd5 14... Nxd5 15. Nxd5 15... cxd5) (11... Qf7 12. a3 12... Na6 13. Nxd5) (11... b5 12. Bb3 12... Kd7 13. dxe5 13... Qg6)
12. Ne4 { Hits the queen and eyes the squares around Black's king. The knight is safe here because the pawn on d4 supports it. [%cal Ge4f6] } 12... Qg6 (12... Qf4 13. Bxf4 13... Nxf4 14. Qf3 14... Be6 15. Bxe6) (12... Nf4 13. Bxf4 13... Qxf4 14. dxe5 14... Bf5 15. Nd6) (12... Qf5 13. dxe5 13... Kd8 14. a3) (12... Qf7 13. a3 13... b5 14. Bb3 14... Na6 15. dxe5) (12... Qe6 13. a3 13... Na6 14. Ng5 14... Qf5 15. g3) (12... Bf5 13. Nxf6 13... gxf6 14. Qh5 14... Ke6)
13. a3 { Kicks the knight on b4, so Black's pieces are driven back. The engine gives White a safe edge of about three-quarters of a pawn. [%cal Ga3b4] } *
